# Prove that ESC at a character-generation menu offers to abandon the
# character, declining restores the same menu, and accepting returns to the
# main menu. This is the stage-1 oracle for inc-gd3c.
#
#   tools/headless.sh tools/keys/chargen-escape.keys 5
#
# WHAT IS BEING PROVED. TextTerm::LMenu ignores ESC unless its caller passes
# MENU_ESC. Character generation historically omitted that flag, leaving a
# player who regretted a choice with no route back to the main menu except
# killing the process. The race menu is the earliest affected menu and proves
# the complete unwind without spending keys on later character choices.
#
# The first ESC must show the abandon question. Answering no must rebuild the
# race option list because LMenu clears it before returning; the second race
# dump proves both the menu prompt and an original race survived that rebuild.
# The second ESC is accepted, and the final dump proves Game::StartMenu is in
# control again rather than a half-created Player entering Game::Play.
#
# The final h is counted from Game::StartMenu's eight visible options in
# src/Main.cpp: Create, Restore, Reincarnate, Recover, Options, Introduction,
# Help, Quit. It exits through the real main-menu command after the oracle has
# been captured.

a
n
y
@dump:race-menu
ESC
@dump:abandon-prompt
n
@dump:race-menu-again
ESC
y
@dump:main-menu
h
